1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,437
The Origins of Halloween.

2
00:00:02,387 --> 00:00:11,362
Halloween derives from the Celtic festival of Samhain, celebrated on October 31, when the boundary between the living and the dead was believed to blur.

3
00:00:11,362 --> 00:00:14,562
Celts wore costumes to ward off spirits.

4
00:00:14,562 --> 00:00:23,075
The Christian church designated November 1 as All Saints Day, and the preceding evening became All Hallows Eve, contracted to Halloween.

5
00:00:23,075 --> 00:00:27,862
Irish immigrants brought Halloween to North America in the mid-19th century.

6
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:34,962
Trick-or-treating evolved from the medieval practice of souling, going door to door offering prayers for the dead in exchange for food.

7
00:00:34,962 --> 00:00:44,425
Jack-o-lanterns originated from an Irish myth about a man who tricked the devil, carved into turnips originally and adapted to pumpkins by Irish immigrants in America.

